# Patron d'installation d'un outil (ex. Vault, MongoDB, ArgoCD)

Chaque outil suit **3 couches** qui collaborent. La règle de référence est `tools/<outil>/install.sh` = **source unique** : Ansible et Terraform ne font que l'appeler.

---

## 1. Couche Helm — `tools/<outil>/`

```
tools/<outil>/
  Chart.yaml       # chart wrapper (dépendance officielle)
  values.yaml      # valeurs par défaut (resources, replicas, service)
  values-demo.yaml # overrides pour le cluster de démo (optionnel)
  install.sh       # script d'install (source unique réutilisée par Ansible)
  README.md        # doc : prérequis, install, accès
```

**`install.sh` — structure type :**
```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -e
SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
cd "$SCRIPT_DIR"

# Guard : kubectl configuré ?
if ! kubectl cluster-info &>/dev/null; then
  echo "Erreur: kubectl ne pointe pas vers un cluster valide."; exit 1
fi

helm repo add <repo> <url> 2>/dev/null || true
helm repo update
kubectl create namespace <ns> --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
helm upgrade --install <release> <chart> -n <ns> -f values.yaml --wait --timeout 10m
echo "Outil installé. Accès via NodePort <port> sur un nœud du cluster."
```

---

## 2. Couche Ansible — `ansible/roles/<outil>_helm/`

```
ansible/roles/<outil>_helm/
  defaults/main.yml   # variables (src, dest, namespace, port, ...)
  tasks/main.yml      # copy tools/, chmod install.sh, run install.sh, cleanup
```

**Pattern de tâches (tasks/main.yml) :**
```yaml
- name: Copy tools/<outil> to remote
  ansible.builtin.copy:
    src: "{{ <outil>_install_src }}"   # ex. playbook_dir + /../tools/<outil>/
    dest: "{{ <outil>_install_dest }}" # ex. /tmp/<outil>-install
    mode: "0644"

- name: Make install.sh executable
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: "{{ <outil>_install_dest }}/install.sh"
    mode: "0755"

- name: Run install script
  ansible.builtin.shell: ./install.sh
  args:
    chdir: "{{ <outil>_install_dest }}"
  environment:
    KUBECONFIG: "{{ ansible_user_dir }}/.kube/config"
  changed_when: true

- name: Cleanup temp directory
  ansible.builtin.file:
    path: "{{ <outil>_install_dest }}"
    state: absent

- name: Show access info
  ansible.builtin.debug:
    msg: "{{ <outil> }} installé sur NodePort {{ <outil>_node_port }}."
```

**defaults/main.yml — variables type :**
```yaml
<outil>_install_src: "{{ playbook_dir }}/../tools/<outil>/"
<outil>_install_dest: /tmp/<outil>-install
<outil>_namespace: <outil>
<outil>_node_port: 3XXXX
```

---

## 3. Couche binaires — `ansible/roles/helm/` (et similaires)

Pour les **binaires CLI** (helm, kubectl, etc.) :

```yaml
# Pattern : stat → skip si déjà installé, sinon : tempfile → get_url → unarchive → copy → cleanup → verify
- name: Check if <bin> is already installed
  ansible.builtin.stat:
    path: "{{ <bin>_install_path }}/<bin>"
  register: _<bin>_installed

- name: Download & install <bin>
  when: not _<bin>_installed.stat.exists
  block:
    - ansible.builtin.tempfile: { state: directory }
      register: _tmp
    - ansible.builtin.get_url:
        url: "https://.../<bin>-{{ <bin>_version }}-{{ <bin>_arch }}.tar.gz"
        dest: "{{ _tmp.path }}/<bin>.tar.gz"
    - ansible.builtin.unarchive:
        src: "{{ _tmp.path }}/<bin>.tar.gz"
        dest: "{{ _tmp.path }}"
        remote_src: true
    - ansible.builtin.copy:
        src: "{{ _tmp.path }}/.../<bin>"
        dest: "{{ <bin>_install_path }}/<bin>"
        mode: "0755"
        remote_src: true
    - ansible.builtin.file: { path: "{{ _tmp.path }}", state: absent }

- name: Verify <bin>
  ansible.builtin.command: <bin> version
  changed_when: false
```

Defaults obligatoires : `<bin>_version`, `<bin>_install_path`, `<bin>_arch`.

